==English==

===Etymology===
From {{af|en|equip|-ment}}, or from {{bor|en|fr|équipement}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɪˈkwɪpmənt/|[ɪˈkʰwɪpmənt]|~|[ɪˈkʰwɪpmn̩t]|a=non-weak vowel}}
** {{audio|en|en-us-equipment.ogg|a=US}}
* {{IPA|en|/əˈkwɪpmənt/|[əˈkwɪpmənt]|~|[əˈkwɪpmn̩t]|a=weak vowel}}
* {{hyph|en|e|quip|ment}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# The act of [[equip]]ping, or the state of being equipped, as for a [[voyage]] or [[expedition]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1756-1761|author=w:David Hume|title=The History of England|passage=The '''equipment''' of the fleet was therefore hastened by de Witt ; in hopes that , by striking at first a successful blow , he might inspire courage into the dismayed States}}
# Any items used in equipping something or someone, for example things needed for an [[expedition]] or [[voyage]].
#: {{usex|en|We need more gardening '''equipment''' if we want to properly landscape our yard, not just a rake and some gloves.}}
#: {{usex|en|The sports shop sells different kits of famous clubs, and '''equipment''' from all kind of sports.}}
#* {{RQ:Longfellow Golden Legend|passage=Armed and [[dight]], In the '''equipments''' of a knight.}}
#* {{RQ:Guardian
|date=11 July 2013|author=Jo Confino|title=How technology has stopped evolution and is destroying the world|url=http://www.guardian.co.uk/sustainable-business/technology-stopped-evolution-destroying-world?INTCMP=SRCH
|passage=Tompkins is considered a hero in the deep ecology movement and works hand in hand with his wife Kris, the former CEO of the outdoor clothing and '''equipment''' company Patagonia.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20261015081305/https://www.theguardian.com/sustainable-business/technology-stopped-evolution-destroying-world?INTCMP=SRCH|archivedate=15 October 2026}}
# {{lb|en|slang|humorous}} The [[male]] [[genitalia]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2018|author=Nicole Seymour|title=Bad Environmentalism|page=93|text=The segment advises the reader matter-of-factly that “the penis [of a whale] should be tucked inside the body and when needed enlarged into an erection”. At the very least, the statement sounds odd. At most, it could make human penis owners consider that their '''equipment''' might not represent the highest evolutionary ideal.}}

